      "title": "Asynchronous Task Orchestration and Fenced Execution in LLM-Driven Workflows",
      "problem": "Long-running LLM generation pipelines in asynchronous worker architectures frequently suffer from worker timeouts, duplicate task redeliveries, and race conditions. When stale or orphaned workers write late-arriving responses back to persistence after cancellation or retry events, they corrupt generation state and waste expensive LLM API tokens.",
      "field": "",
